From a756028c26c93c1a271720105f9d0bab2856a1ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:41:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Node machine: the tests in the machine's own form, at
 reader time, in the shadow

Part of #2524. measure-node-machine --shadow --front-own-tests makes the
bits of the census's set and silence tests from T's records in their
order (node_tests_expression): one loop without a branch on what a
record is, the unit's tables by operator (node_tests_tables, by its
enabled warnings), a byte a record of what it is as an operand, and
three lists: the leaves, the records whose token's parent the tree's
tests read, and the operators that have tests of their own. A constant
operand's tests, a pointer's cast, a string's sum, a comma's discard and
a call's aggregates and callee are exact in place; a record a silence
test may refuse otherwise goes to the census's own code, after a walk
only where that reads a node's parent. With --verify the census's code
runs beside it on every expression: a bit, a span of tokens or a count
of nodes that differs fails the command. --front-tests-last runs either
form after C and X in the timed run.

Shared with the census's code: its walk, its leaf's tests and an
expression's own tests are functions of their own; a type's byte has a
pointer's void pointee and an array; a declaration's three facts are
each made when first asked. The census's reports are the same.

No compile takes it. test-checker: the six census fixtures run in both
forms, the own form beside the census's code.

